The general idea of a codebase cleanup / dead-code analysis tool is a
common one in the ecosystem (e.g. fallow-rs/fallow, Knip, ts-prune). This
plugin was inspired by that category but is an independent, clean-room
implementation with a deliberately different design: it is prompt-driven
and language-agnostic rather than a compiled JS/TS engine, it is strictly
read-only (it reports and ranks, it never edits or deletes), and it tiers
every finding by removal confidence and verifies it against the Code Map.
No upstream code or prose was copied.

